---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import { breadcrumbs } from "../lib/schema";
---
<Base
  title="Verify the Dealer Before You Pay — 5 Checks"
  description="Five checks that separate a real Telegram peptide dealer from a channel with a logo. Batch COA, history depth, vouch dates, reship policy, impostor handles."
  path="/verify/"
  schema={[breadcrumbs([{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Verify", url: "/verify/" }])]}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Do this in two minutes</p>
  <h1>Verify us before you pay a cent</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Telegram has no buyer protection. That is the whole risk, and it is a solvable one. Five checks separate a
    dealer from a channel with a logo. Run them on us, then run them on anyone else you are considering.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Ask for the COA for the exact batch</h2>
  <p>
    Not a COA. The COA for the batch you were quoted. It must carry a lab name and a batch ID, and the batch ID
    must match the vial you receive. A screenshot of a PDF, a COA with a different batch number, or a "COA
    coming" is a fail. Every batch on this desk has a PDF with the lab's own reference number.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Read the history back months</h2>
  <p>
    A handle under three months old has no track record. Scroll the chat. You want to see the same person
    answering the same questions over time, and you want to see price changes that match batch arrivals rather
    than prices that never move.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Check the vouch screenshots are dated and consecutive</h2>
  <p>
    One screenshot cropped nine ways is not evidence. Dated screenshots across months, with different customers,
    are. Ours sit in a pinned album, dated, with the order and the arrival both shown.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Read the reship policy before paying</h2>
  <p>
    Seizures happen. A dealer with no written policy improvises after the fact. Ours is on the
    <a href="/shipping/">shipping page</a>: photograph the notice, we reship once free. Claimed 14 times in four
    years, honoured every time.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Confirm the handle on every page</h2>
  <p>
    Impostors copy the display name and change one character in the handle. The handle on this site is
    <strong>@donjuanjodyy</strong> everywhere, and it is the only handle we take payment through. If someone
    messages you first claiming to be us, check the handle letter by letter.
  </p>

  <h2>What a fail looks like</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Asks for payment before naming a batch.</li>
    <li>Quotes 40 percent under every other band on the market.</li>
    <li>Sends payment details from a second handle.</li>
    <li>Cannot say which lab made the vial.</li>
    <li>Has no channel, only a DM.</li>
  </ul>

  <CTA
    src="/verify/"
    label="Verify page"
    heading="Checked us out? The desk is open."
    body="Message @donjuanjodyy with the peptide and your country. Price, batch ID and COA inside 90 seconds."
  />
</Base>